From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSBedded <noreply@jsbedded.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Move the embed glue into src/embed and list the embed
 sources

Not sent upstream yet (upstream ask 4 in JSBedded's
firmware/engines/ant/README.md).

The stubs that make the interpreter-only build link (no ESM, timers,
events, Date or Buffer; the microtask queue; the JIT entry points; the
filesystem helpers) live in packages/wasm/src/ and include
wasm_embed.h, so an embedder outside Meson has to copy them.

- packages/wasm/src/{stubs,jit_stub,utils}.c move to src/embed/ and
  include embed.h. Only bridge.c and platform.c stay Wasm-specific.
- sources.json gets an "embed" group: the core, GC, Silver, the
  built-ins the reactor initialises and src/embed/*.c, as a plain file
  list that CMake, ESP-IDF or pico-sdk builds can read without Meson.
  It matches the reactor's core_sources.
- Error messages say "this embed build" instead of "@antjs.org/wasm".
